Constructing Frank Lloyd Wright's vision of a spiral museum was not an easy feat to pull off. Right oversaw the work, but a local architect named William Short was in charge of the project on the ground, and George Cohen was the general contractor. In the three years it took to build the Guggenheim. They came to the realization that some of Wright's ideas were not going to be doable. Like the idea of making the building a self-supporting spiral. If you imagine a slinky or something in the way that the wire,
实现弗兰克·劳埃德·赖特关于螺旋博物馆的构想绝非易事。赖特监督了这项工作，但一位名叫威廉·肖特 (William Short) 的当地建筑师负责现场项目，乔治·科恩 (George Cohen) 则是总承包商。在建造古根海姆的三时间里，他们意识到赖的一些想法是无法实现的。比如将建筑做成一个自支撑螺旋的想法。如果你想象一个弹力玩具或类似的东西，电线由于处于那种张力中而将自身维系在一起，他在早期就是这么说的。

