of lines that betray the form of the plywood molds that created the shape of the outer wall. They had hired a subcontractor to do the gunite and because they didn't think about the formwork being expressed, the gunite formwork is placed on like a real angle which is not consistent. It's just because they didn't think you would see it, and so they just made their pattern work as you do. The pattern is a result of the gun-ite construction, and Frank Lloyd Wright didn't like the fact that it was visible.
